## Part F: Timeline [{{ c.process_cite }}]

- Notice: the Investigating Officer issues notice to the account holder(s) within 7 calendar days [{{ c.process_cite }}].
- Reply: the account holder replies within 15 days of the notice.
- Remittance: on the direction to release, the bank remits the attributed amounts within 15 days and updates CFCFRMS [SOP-5-XIII].

## Part G: Escalation flags (human decision required)

{% for e in c.escalations %}
- A/c No. {{ s[e.acct ~ "/account_id"] }} is flagged ESCALATE_S106_CANDIDATE because {{ e.basis }}. The hold of {{ s[e.acct ~ "/hold_amount"] }} stays amount-specific and restoration can proceed. Seizure under Section 106 BNSS needs a registered FIR and a debit freeze needs an order of the Magistrate under Section 107 BNSS [BNSS-106] [BNSS-107]; banks may only mark the disputed amount under lien [CASE-KARTIK-CHATUR]. The nodal officer decides on any escalation.
{% else %}
